#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
NLM (Neural Learning Machine) - High-level Python API

This module provides a comprehensive, user-friendly interface for the NLM neural simulation framework.
It builds upon the low-level C++ bindings to provide:
- Intuitive, Pythonic APIs for common operations
- Comprehensive error handling and validation
- Convenience methods for typical use cases
- Rich documentation and examples
- Integration with standard Python ecosystem

Example usage:

    import nlm

    # Create a simple brain
    brain = nlm.create_brain()
    brain.initialize()

    # Run simulation with convenience methods
    brain.run_simulation(100)

    # Use agent in world
    agent = nlm.create_agent(brain)
    world = nlm.create_world()
    world.configure(width=20, height=20)
    
    # Run complete episode
    episode_reward = agent.run_episode(world, max_steps=500)
    
    print(f"Episode completed with reward: {episode_reward}")

The NLM brain operates as a closed-loop system:

WORLD
  ↓
SENSORY INPUT
  ↓
NEURAL PROCESSING (LIF dynamics, spikes)
  ↓
INTERNAL STATE (working memory, attention)
  ↓
MEMORY / PREDICTION
  ↓
MOTIVATION / NEUROMODULATION (dopamine, curiosity)
  ↓
ACTION SELECTION
  ↓
MOTOR OUTPUT
  ↓
WORLD CONSEQUENCE
  ↓
REWARD / SURPRISE / ERROR
  ↓
PLASTICITY (STDP, Hebbian, structural)
  ↓
MEMORY / DEVELOPMENT
  ↓
CHANGED BRAIN
  ↓
CHANGED FUTURE BEHAVIOR
"""

